WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.910
The Marvel Cinematic Universe has done an
amazing job of linking up numerous films and

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:07.200
characters in a fairly cohesive world.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:11.570
But for all the work Marvel has put into making
the stories seem real and fully fleshed out,

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:14.820
there are still a few things going on that
have us scratching our heads — at least

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:15.820
for now.

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:19.279
Here are six MCU mysteries we're still trying
to comprehend.

00:00:19.279 --> 00:00:20.330
Alternate universes

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:24.829
The introduction of Quicksilver in Avengers:
Age of Ultron also introduced a whole bucket

00:00:24.829 --> 00:00:29.110
of confusion, considering a different version
of Quicksilver is also appearing in Fox's

00:00:29.110 --> 00:00:30.500
line of X-Men films.

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:34.130
Now, we know that in the real world, this
is because of licensing shenanigans between

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:37.480
Marvel's parent company, Disney, and 20th
Century Fox.

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:39.990
But could there be deeper implications for
these fictional worlds?

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:44.190
Are there alternate versions of other heroes
that could also cross over between franchises?

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:47.760
Or is it possible we could even see a crossover
between the Avengers and the X-Men, or the

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:48.760
Fantastic Four?

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:52.260
If they all exist in the same multi-verse,
it's possible they could interact in the same

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:54.860
way the TV versions of Flash and Supergirl
do.

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:59.640
Let's not forget, Marvel worked out a deal
to share Spider-Man with Sony, and Fox negotiated

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:02.260
a character rights trade with Marvel shortly
afterward.

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:07.159
If the X-Men and Avengers could actually crossover...well,
that would be an awesome cliffhanger to end

00:01:07.159 --> 00:01:08.530
Avengers: Infinity War...

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:09.530
Atlantis

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:13.960
At the end of Iron Man 2, Tony Stark meets
with Nick Fury at a SHIELD outpost.

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:17.920
In the background, there's a map that has
certain areas marked as points of interest,

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:22.549
including a spot in New Mexico for Thor, Wakanda
in Africa for the Black Panther, and then

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:24.710
a random spot in the middle of the ocean.

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:28.359
This seemed to be a pretty obvious reference
for Atlantis, the underwater kingdom ruled

00:01:28.359 --> 00:01:31.200
by one of Marvel's oldest heroes, Prince Namor,
the Sub-Mariner.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:35.430
But so far, while all the other teasers hidden
in that scene have played out on screen, there

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:37.900
has been no sign of Namor or Atlantis.

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:40.090
So does Atlantis exist in the MCU?

00:01:40.090 --> 00:01:42.509
Is it hanging with the Fantastic Four over
at Fox?

00:01:42.509 --> 00:01:44.350
Or is there some other secret beneath the
waves?

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:45.899
Only time will tell.

00:01:45.899 --> 00:01:47.200
The Red Skull's fate

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:52.329
In Captain America: The First Avenger, the
Red Skull powers his weapons using the Tesseract,

00:01:52.329 --> 00:01:55.450
which is an Infinity Stone that acts as a
doorway to another world.

00:01:55.450 --> 00:01:59.889
During his final fight with Captain America,
the Red Skull grabs the Tesseract and vanishes.

00:01:59.889 --> 00:02:01.280
He's never been heard from again.

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:02.280
So what happened to him?

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:06.009
We know from Thor that the Tesseract connects
to the Nine Realms through the World Tree,

00:02:06.009 --> 00:02:08.250
and when Loki entered the World Tree, he survived.

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:12.760
We also know from Avengers that the alien
bad guys can also be reached through the Tesseract's

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:13.760
portal.

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:15.510
Is the Red Skull working with Thanos?

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:17.050
Did he end up lost somewhere in Asgard?

00:02:17.050 --> 00:02:19.260
Or did the Tesseract send him somewhere else?

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:20.260
Hmm.

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:21.780
That's my confused noise.

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:23.440
What happened in Budapest?

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:27.720
Black Widow and Hawkeye from the Avengers
have one of the tightest bonds in the MCU,

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:31.000
forged in part through a traumatic shared
experience on a mission in Budapest.

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:33.960
"Just like Budapest all over again!"

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:36.840
"You and I remember Budapest very differently."

00:02:36.849 --> 00:02:38.760
But what exactly happened in Budapest?

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:42.430
We know from Captain America: Winter Soldier
that whatever happened there was major enough

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:45.340
that members of the World Security Council
had been briefed on it.

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:48.590
"If you do this none of your past is gonna
remain hidden.

00:02:48.590 --> 00:02:50.440
Not Budapest, not Osaka..."

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:54.069
And we know it affected both Black Widow and
Hawkeye for years afterwards.

00:02:54.069 --> 00:02:58.310
In other words, it's a pretty big deal — but
exactly how big is something Marvel has yet

00:02:58.310 --> 00:02:59.310
to reveal.

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:01.150
Who is the real Mandarin?

00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:05.390
Hardcore comic book fans were over the moon
when it was announced that Tony Stark's archenemy,

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:09.069
The Mandarin, would be the bad guy in Iron
Man 3, especially since the character had

00:03:09.069 --> 00:03:13.460
been teased way back in the first Iron Man
film with references to the "ten rings" terrorist

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:14.460
organization.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:17.689
So fans were aghast when it turned out that
the Mandarin wasn't all he was cracked up

00:03:17.689 --> 00:03:18.689
to be.

00:03:18.689 --> 00:03:20.640
"My name's Trevor, Trevor Slattery."

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:22.820
"What are you?

00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:25.940
What are you a decoy, you're a double right?"

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:28.030
"Well no absolutely not."

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:31.100
"Don't hurt the face I'm an actor!"

00:03:31.109 --> 00:03:36.409
Fan backlash was so strong that Marvel filmed
a DVD one-shot for the Iron Man 3 DVD where

00:03:36.409 --> 00:03:40.500
Slattery is kidnapped by people claiming to
be agents for the real Mandarin.

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:43.310
"You see there's somebody who wants to meet
you."

00:03:43.310 --> 00:03:45.040
"Do I know him?"

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:50.110
"No, but you took his name, and now he wants
it back."

00:03:50.110 --> 00:03:51.819
And then… that's been it.

00:03:51.819 --> 00:03:54.280
So is there really a true bad guy called the
Mandarin?

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:56.120
And will we ever see him on screen?

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:57.739
Fans are still waiting to find out.

00:03:57.739 --> 00:03:59.720
Why are there two Infinity Gauntlets?

00:03:59.720 --> 00:04:04.290
In the mid-credits scene of Avengers: Age
of Ultron, Thanos opens a vault and puts on

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:06.019
the Infinity Gauntlet.

00:04:06.019 --> 00:04:10.179
"Fine, I'll do it myself."

00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:16.400
Which is a little weird, because back in Thor,
we saw that Odin had the Infinity Gauntlet

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:18.280
safely hidden away in his vault.

00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:19.280
The explanation?

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:23.880
Well, according to Marvel Studios president
Kevin Feige, "There are two different gloves,"

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:24.880
one for each hand.

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:28.850
That kind of makes sense, but Marvel producer
Jeremy Latcham muddied the waters when he

00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:32.400
suggested in an interview that one of the
gauntlets is actually fake.

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:34.530
So why is there a fake Infinity Gauntlet?

00:04:34.530 --> 00:04:37.970
And which one is real — the one Thanos has,
or the one Odin has?

00:04:37.970 --> 00:04:42.250
With Avengers: Infinity War fast approaching,
this is finally one question fans can actually

00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:44.919
expect an answer to sooner rather than later.

00:04:44.919 --> 00:04:45.919
Thanks for watching!

